  "title": "Andrew R NDE 3469",
  "date": "April 28 2002",
  "content": "My car had flipped and while it was happening I heard glass breaking and other noises but then it went calm. It was different from being knocked out, I then woke up, or believed I woke up, and climbed out of the vehicle and to the top of the hill where I had flipped. I then tried to stop passing cars but no one seemed to see me. I then went back into the car because it was still running so I thought I should turn it off, that's when I saw what I believed was my own body. At that time, I woke up climbed out of the car again and up the hill. That's when a passing motorist stopped to help at which time I seemed to feel as though I didn't want her help, I felt angry and mad. And ever since that day I seem to be more violent and snap for no reason sometimes. I believe this event brought out some sort of dark side in me; it has even cost me a relationship of four years. My anger and violence has even got me in trouble with the police. And up to this event I never did the things that I have done since then in regards to the violent behavior.",
